# Frontend Chat UI

## Identity

This is the **public-facing** Litecoin Knowledge Hub chat interface, served at `chat.lite.space/chat`. End users interact with the RAG assistant through this UI. It is NOT the admin dashboard.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology | Version |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| Framework | Next.js | 15.5.8 |
| React | React | 19 |
| UI Components | Shadcn UI | configured (`components.json` present) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS | v4 |
| Animation | Framer Motion | latest |
| Markdown | react-markdown | latest |
| Rich Text | TipTap | (for CMS article editor in `components/cms/`) |
| Validation | Zod + react-hook-form | latest |

## Key Conventions

### Component Library

Shadcn UI components live in `components/ui/`. To add a new component:

```bash
npx shadcn-ui@latest add <component-name>
```

Do NOT hand-roll components that Shadcn provides. Do NOT copy Shadcn patterns into `admin-frontend/` — it uses bare Radix without Shadcn.

### Routing & Base Path

The app uses `basePath: '/chat'` in `next.config.ts`. All internal links and API calls are relative to this base path. Never hardcode absolute URLs to the backend.

### API Communication

Next.js rewrites proxy API calls to the backend:

```
/api/v1/:path* → ${BACKEND_URL}/api/v1/:path*
```

Always use relative fetch paths like `/api/v1/chat/stream`. The backend URL is resolved by the rewrite config, not by client code.

### Streaming Protocol

Chat responses use `ReadableStream` + `TextDecoder` with SSE-style JSON lines:

```
data: {"status": "thinking", ...}\n
data: {"status": "thinking", "stage": "searching" | "checking_live_data" | "writing"}\n
data: {"status": "streaming", "chunk": "chunk..."}\n
data: {"status": "complete", "requestId": "...", ...}\n
data: {"status": "follow_ups", "questions": [...], "requestId": "..."}\n   # trails complete
```

Event types to handle: `thinking`, `streaming`, `sources`, `follow_ups`, `complete`, `error`, `usage_status`, `blockchain_data`.

- `thinking` may carry `stage`; `StreamingMessage.tsx` shows the label beside the dots. Do not flip a `streaming` message back to `thinking` on a late marker.
- `complete` comes **before** `follow_ups` (follow-ups are a second LLM call). Unlock the composer on `complete`, keep reading, and attach `follow_ups` to the message whose `requestId` matches (it may already have moved from the streaming slot into `messages`).
- `sources` carries structured chips `{payload_id, title, url, updated_at, last_reviewed_at, stale, tier}` built server-side from retrieval metadata (`SourceChips.tsx`). Never parse citations out of the answer text.
- `complete` carries `isGrounded`, `webSources` (unverified web chips), `abstained`, `requestId` (needed by `AnswerFeedback.tsx` to POST `/api/v1/chat/feedback`), `earlyType`, `incidentPinId`.
- `blockchain_data.data._provenance` = `{source, endpoint, fetched_at}`; `BlockchainDataRenderer` renders it under every live card. `data_type: "metric"` is a litview.space on-chain metric (`MetricCard.tsx` + `Sparkline.tsx`); `status: "not_computed"` must render as "no value yet", never as 0.

Challenges are one-time use: `page.tsx` keeps one prefetched spare (`spareChallengeRef`), uses it at send, and re-arms right after the POST returns. On 403 `invalid_challenge`, fetch a new challenge from `/api/v1/auth/challenge` and retry once. The conversation is mirrored to `sessionStorage` (`lkh:chat:messages:v1`); the chat body may include `category_hint` (landing-page topic id).

### Authentication

The public frontend uses **fingerprint challenge-response** for rate limiting — NOT Bearer tokens. Auth flow:

1. `GET /api/v1/auth/challenge` → receive challenge
2. Include `X-Fingerprint` header on subsequent requests

There is no login page, no user accounts, no `localStorage` tokens in this frontend.

### Content Sources

- **Suggested questions + categories**: `GET /api/v1/suggested-questions` on the backend (one request via the `/api/v1` rewrite; returns `categories`, `questions` with `cached` flags). `SuggestedQuestions.tsx` orchestrates `landing/TopicPicker.tsx` → `landing/QuestionGrid.tsx`; it falls back to the flat grid when there are no categories. Do not call Payload directly from the browser.
- **Chat responses**: Streamed from backend via `/api/v1/chat/stream`

### CMS Components

`components/cms/` contains an article editor (TipTap-based) with `ArticleEditor.tsx`, `FrontmatterForm.tsx`, `TiptapEditor.tsx`. These are part of the public frontend for content contribution workflows.

## Forbidden

- Never import from `admin-frontend/` — these are completely separate applications
- Never use Bearer token auth patterns — that is admin-only
- Never hardcode `localhost:8000` or any backend URL in client code
- Never use `getServerSideProps` patterns from older Next.js — this is App Router (Next.js 15)
